    "body": "<h2 id=\"h_01HZJ9C64033Q1N2NF4WWZJ30E\">You will learn</h2>\n<p>Learn how to take a random sample from a list or segment in Klaviyo. This can be useful when running a contest or giveaway, or when you'd like to send a message to a random subset of an audience. </p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HZJ9C640SM3MXP4WDT6CANX1\">Take a random sample of a list or segment</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Navigate to <strong>Audience &gt; Lists &amp; segments</strong> tab of your account. </li>\n<li>Click a list or segment.</li>\n<li>In the upper right-hand corner of your screen, click either:\n<ul>\n<li>\n<strong>Manage Segment &gt; Sample Segment Members</strong> (for a segment).<br>or </li>\n<li>\n<strong>Manage List &gt; Sample list members </strong>(for a list).<br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/32431685889691\" alt=\"The Sample List Members option in Klaviyo\">\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Input how many people you would like to be included in this sample in the <em>Sample size</em> field.<br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/32431685894683\" alt=\"The sample creation modal for a list\">\n</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Create List</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"bs-callout bs-callout-default\">\n<p>The new list created with the random sample of profiles will have <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115005251108\">double opt-in</a> enabled by default. </p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HZJ9C6406G2PZEYR07GDADNW\" class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-left\">Additional resources</h2>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/115005061447\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Understanding the difference between segments and lists</a></li>\n<li class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/360043947571\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Understanding the benefits of having a main list for each channel</a></li>\n</ul>",
    "user_segment_ids": []
  },
